,"text":"Use this method to clean up after components that are gone, such as removing an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"entity’s health bar when it loses its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Health"},{"type":"text","text":". The first call for a type starts recording"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its removals ("},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/trackRemovals(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":"), so removals made before it aren’t reported. Each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reader type has its own place in the record, as with "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/readEvents(_:by:)"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["enum HealthbarReader {}","","var world = World()","_ = world.removed(Health.self, by: HealthbarReader.self)","","let knight = world.spawn(Health(current: 10))","let archer = world.spawn(Health(current: 6))","world.remove(Health.self, from: archer)","world.despawn(knight)","","let lost = world.removed(Health.self, by: HealthbarReader.self)","print(lost == [archer, knight])","\/\/ Prints \"true\""],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An entity appears once per removal: an entity whose "},{"code":"C","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is removed, inserted and removed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"again appears twice."}]},{"type":"aside","style":"note","name":"Complexity","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"O("},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"r","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":"), where "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"r","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" is the number of removals returned."}]}]}]}],"references":{"doc://WorldModule/documentation/WorldModule":{"url":"\/documentation\/wor